    "though the next turn will have nothing else.\n\n"
    + TURN_TAIL
)


# A REVISION IS A TURN, AND IT IS NOT PART OF THE LESSON.
#
# Feedback on a document comes off the library page, which is not a sitting: it
# never writes to `live/cards/`, never archives the lesson and never changes
# `state.json`, because somebody mid-proof on an iPad must not be interrupted by
# somebody correcting a deck.
#
# That is the whole reason this turn RUNS FRESH. `turn_plan` resumes the agent's
# conversation by default, and a revision resumed into a lesson drags the lesson
# into the document and the document back into the lesson. The alternative was a
# second daemon per workspace, which doubles the cost and the failure modes for a
# turn that takes a minute.
#
# So it is its own session, it writes no card, and its report goes back beside
# the document rather than onto the glass.
HEADLESS_REVISE_PROMPT = (
    "You are running headless, and THIS TURN IS NOT PART OF THE LESSON. Nobody "
    "is waiting at a board for a card. Somebody read a document this workspace "
    "has written and said what is wrong with it, from the library page.\n\n"
    "They sent this:\n\n%(inbox)s\n\n"
    "Do this, and nothing else:\n"
    "1. Read the feedback file the text above names, and read the document it is "
    "about. Both are paths in this repository.\n"
    "2. REVISE THE DOCUMENT. Edit the source the document is built from -- the "
    "`.tex` or the `.md` beside it -- and rebuild the PDF if it has one. Keep "
    "its structure, its names for things and its claims except where the "
    "feedback says otherwise. Do not start it again and do not widen it.\n"
    "3. Write what you changed at the BOTTOM OF THE FEEDBACK FILE, under a "
    "`## What was changed` heading: what you changed, what you left and why, "
    "and anything in the feedback you could not act on. That file is the record "
    "of this round and it is where the person who wrote the feedback will look.\n\n"
    "**Write no card.** Do not run `board write`, do not run `board open`, do "
    "not touch `live/state.json`, `live/cards/` or `HANDOFF.md`, and do not run "
    "`board wait`. There is a lesson on this board and it belongs to somebody "
    "else's evening; this turn must leave every part of it exactly as it found "
    "it.\n\n"
    "Do not read `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `live/TEACHING.md` or the cards: none of "
    "them is about this document. `board brief` is not needed either. End the "
    "turn when the document and the feedback file are both written."
)


# AN OVERHAUL IS THE OTHER ASK ON THE SAME PANEL, AND IT IS NOT A REVISION.
#
# `HEADLESS_REVISE_PROMPT` above says to keep the document's structure, its names
# for things and its claims: "Do not start it again and do not widen it." That is
# exactly right for "figure 3 is mislabelled" and exactly wrong for "that
# presentation needs an overhaul now that we plan to use colibri" -- and until
# there was a second ask, the only route to an overhaul was a terminal.
#
# SO THE DO-NOT-WIDEN SENTENCE IS NOT IN HERE, and that is the whole of the
# difference. What replaces it is a brief: the feedback file carries a sentence
# saying what the document is FOR now, and that sentence outranks the shape the
# document presently has.
#
# THE UNDO IS GIT, AND IT IS ALREADY IN PLACE BEFORE THIS TURN RUNS. An overhaul
# replaces thirty-three pages. `/library/feedback` refuses a rework whose source
# is uncommitted -- see `tutorboard/leaving.py` -- so this turn starts from a
# committed source by construction and the whole overhaul is one diff. It is told
# so, because a turn that thinks it has no undo hedges.
HEADLESS_REWORK_PROMPT = (
    "You are running headless, and THIS TURN IS NOT PART OF THE LESSON. Nobody "
    "is waiting at a board for a card. Somebody read a document this workspace "
    "has written and asked for it to be OVERHAULED, from the library page.\n\n"
    "They sent this:\n\n%(inbox)s\n\n"
    "Do this, and nothing else:\n"
    "1. Read the feedback file the text above names, and read the document it is "
    "about. Both are paths in this repository. The feedback file has a `## What "
    "this document is FOR now` section: that is the brief, and it outranks the "
    "shape the document presently has.\n"
    "2. REWORK THE DOCUMENT to that purpose. Edit the source it is built from -- "
    "the `.tex` or the `.md` beside it -- and rebuild the PDF if it has one. Its "
    "structure, its section order, its length and what it covers are all yours "
    "to change: restructure it, cut what the new purpose does not need, reorder "
    "what it does, and rewrite. Keep it the same KIND of document -- a deck stays "
    "a deck and a paper stays a paper -- and keep anything the brief does not "
    "touch. LEAVE THE FILE WHERE IT IS, under the name it has: the library names "
    "a document by its path, and the marks somebody has drawn on its pages are "
    "anchored to that name. The source is committed as it stands, so this "
    "overhaul is one diff and reverting it costs nothing; work accordingly "
    "rather than hedging.\n"
    "3. Write what you changed at the BOTTOM OF THE FEEDBACK FILE, under a "
    "`## What was changed` heading: what the document is now, what you cut and "
    "why, and anything in the brief you could not act on. That file is the "
    "record of this round and it is where the person who asked will look.\n\n"
    "**Write no card.** Do not run `board write`, do not run `board open`, do "
    "not touch `live/state.json`, `live/cards/` or `HANDOFF.md`, and do not run "
    "`board wait`. There is a lesson on this board and it belongs to somebody "
    "else's evening; this turn must leave every part of it exactly as it found "
    "it.\n\n"
    "Do not read `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `live/TEACHING.md` or the cards: none of "
    "them is about this document. `board brief` is not needed either. End the "
    "turn when the document and the feedback file are both written."
)


# A DOCUMENT ASKED FOR MID-SITTING IS A TURN, AND IT IS NOT PART OF THE LESSON.
#
# Asked for as a question -- "at any point can I have a presentation or paper
# written up going through the things we talked about in that tutoring session?
# Can I do that in ANY tutoring session?" -- and the answer was no, because
# asking meant changing the sitting's AIM and the aim row is withheld from a
# review and a walkthrough.
#
# `POST /writeup` is the act that changes no aim. Which makes this turn's whole
# problem the one a revision already has: there is a lesson on this board and it
# belongs to somebody's evening, so a deck's slides must not stream into a
# transcript somebody is mid-proof in. It runs FRESH for that reason and writes
# no card; the document appears in the LIBRARY, where correcting it is already a
# loop that exists.
#
# WHAT IT IS ABOUT AND HOW TO WRITE IT ARE BOTH IN THE INBOX LINE, not here --
# `sense.writeup_sense` carries the scope and appends `sense.MAKE_SENSE` whole,
# so the rules about a document are in one place rather than two that drift.
HEADLESS_WRITEUP_PROMPT = (
    "You are running headless, and THIS TURN IS NOT PART OF THE LESSON. Nobody "
    "is waiting at a board for a card. Somebody asked, from the sitting open on "
    "this board, for a document to be written.\n\n"
    "%(inbox)s\n\n"
    "Do what the text above says, and nothing else. It names the product, what "
    "the document is about, and where the file goes; follow it exactly. Where it "
    "says the scope is the concepts this sitting covered, `board recap --all` is "
    "how you read the lesson back -- one call, not one per card.\n\n"
    "**Write no card.** Do not run `board write`, do not run `board open`, do "
    "not touch `live/state.json`, `live/cards/` or `HANDOFF.md`, and do not run "
    "`board wait`. The sitting on this board is somebody's evening and its aim "
